## Orchestrator Output — Repository Result Pattern (REFACTOR-RESULT-2026-06-11) — 2026-06-11

### Goal
Refactor the repository layer from throw/null-on-failure to an explicit `Result<T, E>` discriminated union so that "not found" and "unique-constraint conflict" become typed, value-returned outcomes instead of thrown exceptions (or silent nulls). Services unwrap the Result and continue to throw the same typed domain errors upward, so route-observable behavior (404 on not-found, 409 on conflict) is byte-for-byte preserved. Zero behavior change; all 543 tests must pass WITHOUT modification.

SECURITY_REVIEW: REQUIRED
SECURITY_REASON: Refactor is intended zero-logic-change, BUT it edits src/auth/auth.repository.ts — a mandatory CATCH-ALL trigger (src/auth/*). Auth error-path parity matters: a refactor that changes which error type/timing surfaces on the refresh-token reuse/not-found path could weaken ADR-012 reuse-detection or introduce a user/token enumeration oracle. Scoped differential review required (error-path parity only).
SECURITY_STATUS: PENDING (security-engineer Phase 1 — gates auth-touching parts of Phase 2)

### Scope
IN: NEW src/shared/result.ts (Result type + ok/err constructors + minimal unwrap helpers, no deps); convert repository methods that can return "not found" → Result<T, NotFoundError> and methods that can fail unique-constraint → Result<T, ConflictError>, across tasks/users/auth/urls repositories (admin.repository.ts ALSO in scope — it shares the identical pattern: P2002 on addBlockedDomain, P2025 on reviewFlagged/deleteFlagged, null on findFlaggedById — architect to confirm consistency); service layer unwraps Result and throws the SAME typed errors it throws today.
OUT: any change to routes, error-handler, or HTTP status mapping; any new dependency; any test-file modification (HARD STOP if a test needs editing); any change to method semantics beyond the throw→Result transport; performance/transaction redesign.

### Constraints (frozen)
- Result type lives in src/shared/result.ts (NEW). Shape: `type Result<T,E> = { ok:true; value:T } | { ok:false; error:E }`. NO `any` (slop script P1-fails on `: any` / `as any`).
- No new dependencies.
- ALL 543 existing tests pass WITHOUT modification. A test requiring edit ⇒ behavior change ⇒ STOP that path and escalate. Tests test behavior, not implementation.
- Cyclomatic complexity must NOT increase per-file vs .quality-baseline.json (v1.2.0). Repos baseline: tasks.repository.ts=18, users.repository.ts=8, auth.repository.ts=2, urls.repository.ts=3, admin.repository.ts (not separately listed — treat as additive watch). Degradation rule: >50% file complexity increase = automatic P1.
- ADR-010/011 layering preserved: repositories remain the only Prisma importers; services own the unwrap+throw; routes/error-handler untouched.

### CRITICAL CONTEXT (orchestrator pre-read of all 5 repos — architect/backend-dev MUST reconcile)
The current repos do NOT uniformly "throw on not found". Actual current pattern:
- Reads already return `T | null` (findById, findByEmail, findByCode, findByHash, findFlaggedById, findPublicById, findByGoogleId) — NOT throwing.
- Boolean probes: existsById, isBlocked return boolean.
- Mutations via Prisma `.update()` / `.delete()` (tasks.update/delete, auth.revokeById, urls.recordClick/delete, admin.reviewFlagged/deleteFlagged) DO throw Prisma P2025 when the row is absent.
- Creates that can collide: urls.create + admin.addBlockedDomain rely on the SERVICE catching Prisma P2002 (ADR-022). users.create / createFromOAuth similarly. tasks.create cannot conflict.
- linkGoogleAccount + removeBlockedDomain + revokeFamily already return count/null (no throw).
This means the architect must DEFINE precisely which methods convert to Result and how the existing null-returning reads map (option: keep reads as-is OR fold null→Result<_,NotFoundError>; must be chosen so NO test changes). The load-bearing risk: services currently branch on `=== null` and on `catch (P2002/P2025)`. The unwrap must reproduce the exact same thrown error so route status is unchanged. This is a PATTERN decision (ADR), architect-owned; tech-lead NOT needed unless architect flags a conflict (e.g. needing a new dep or a behavior change).

### Agent Execution Plan
Phase 1 (design): architect — short ADR (ADR-044) defining the Result boundary: which repo methods return Result, how P2002→ConflictError / P2025|null→NotFoundError map, how services unwrap, and the rule that keeps all 543 tests unchanged. Records rationale. Flags to orchestrator if a new dep or behavior change is unavoidable.
Phase 2 (security, SCOPED differential): security-engineer — auth error-path parity ONLY (auth.repository.ts findByHash/createToken/revokeById/revokeFamily + auth.service unwrap): confirm no behavior/timing/enumeration change in refresh reuse-detection (ADR-012) and login. Gates the auth portion of Phase 3. (Runs after architect so the boundary is known; light/tight.)
Phase 3 (impl): backend-dev — create result.ts; convert repos per ADR-044; unwrap in services; run tsc + vitest, confirm 543/543 with ZERO test files touched; report git diff --stat proving no *test* file changed. GATED on security-engineer DONE for auth parts.
Phase 4 (review, parallel): qa-engineer ‖ code-quality.
Phase 5 (gate): quality-lead — explicit SHIP IT required.
Phase 6 (docs): tech-writer — CHANGELOG note only (internal refactor; no public API change) UNLESS public docs reference repo behavior.

COLLAPSED (justified): tech-lead (no new dependency, no stack change — pure internal pattern within frozen ADR-010 layering; architect owns the pattern ADR). data-lead + db-engineer (no schema/migration/index change — transport-only refactor over existing queries). frontend/mobile/devops/ai/ml (untouched domains). ESCALATION VALVE: if backend-dev finds it CANNOT preserve all 543 tests without editing a test, or needs a new dep, or the unwrap forces a behavior change → STOP and escalate.

### Open Questions
1. Do the already-null-returning reads convert to Result, or stay null? (architect decides — must keep tests green.) 2. Is admin.repository.ts in the conversion or noted-as-consistent-followup? (architect rules; orchestrator leans IN for consistency.) Neither blocks Phase 1.

### Hierarchy Execution Log
| Phase | Agent | Tier | Status | Task |
|-------|-------|------|--------|------|
| 1 | architect | 3 | DONE (resolved) | ADR-044 written. 27/31 methods STAY (reads already return null — no throw to remove; P2025 mutation paths dead-guarded by find-then-assert in services). Only 4 P2002 creates are real throw→Result candidates. Tests pin thrown-P2002 at create seam → converting breaks ~6-10 tests. "Zero-test-change" vs "convert conflict methods" were MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE. ESCALATED to user. |
| 1b | orchestrator | 1 | DONE | Independently verified architect's claim against test files: mockRejectedValue(uniqueViolation()) P2002 confirmed at urls.service.test.ts:125/137, admin.service.test.ts:95, google-oauth.service.test.ts:208-258. Architect ruling sound. HOLDING for user A-vs-B decision before Phase 2/3. |
| 1c | orchestrator (RESUME 2026-06-11) | 1 | DONE | USER RULED: Option B creates-only. Re-verified baseline myself: tsc exit 0, vitest 543/543 (40 test files), src/shared/result.ts absent, ConflictError+NotFoundError present in errors.ts. Re-read all 4 repos + 4 services + 3 conflict test files. KEY NUANCE captured for backend-dev: (a) register() at auth.service.ts:75-83 has NO try/catch on users.create today — unwrap must add `if(!r.ok) throw r.error`; (b) guardUniqueGoogleId STAYS (still guards linkGoogleAccount P2002 throw — link is NOT converted) but createOAuthAccount must unwrap createFromOAuth's Result; (c) non-P2002 passthrough tests (urls:145, admin:108, goauth:234) STAY as rejections; (d) urls retry test:124-126 is a MIX (rejectOnce→resolveOnce) → becomes resolveOnce(err)→resolveOnce(ok). ADR-044 status → ACCEPTED Option B. NOTE: .quality-baseline.json is STALE at 501 tests/37 files — code-quality must correct to 543/40. |
| 2 | security-engineer | 3 | PENDING | SCOPED differential: users/auth create path P2002 narrowing + oauth create/link parity |
| 3 | backend-dev | 3 | PENDING | Option B: result.ts + 4 create-method conversion + 4 service unwraps + bounded conflict-path test edits; 543/543; diff --stat |
| 4 | qa-engineer ‖ code-quality | 3 | PENDING | parallel review (see rows below) |
| 2 | security-engineer | 3 | PENDING | SCOPED differential: auth error-path parity (no timing/enumeration change, ADR-012 intact) |
| 3 | backend-dev | 3 | PENDING | result.ts + repo conversion + service unwrap; 543/543 unchanged; diff proves no test edited |
