## Security-Engineer Output — Repository Result Pattern (REFACTOR-RESULT-2026-06-11) — 2026-06-11

### Context-budget compliance
- Tags grepped in brief.md: `agent: security-engineer`, `domain: security`, `domain: architecture` (grep returned hits at lines 78, 114/421, 1552/1629, 1872/1898, 2487/2656, 3573/3598, 3683/3817, 4540/4702, 5159/5217, 5221/5266, **5283–5288 (directed placeholder)**, 5295). Read ONLY the directed target window brief.md **5283–5412** (~130 of 5412 lines, ~2.4%). decisions.md: read ONLY ADR-044 (lines 1015–1105) as directed — the binding spec.
- Source read (all in-scope, in-diff): full `git diff` of the 6 named files; `src/shared/result.ts`; `auth.service.ts` 125–240 (OAuth ladder). Confirmed untouched files by absence from `git diff --name-only`.

### Scope / risk classification (differential)
- HIGH RISK reviewed in full: `src/auth/auth.service.ts` (auth create path), `src/users/users.repository.ts` (user/OAuth create).
- MEDIUM: `src/urls/urls.repository.ts`, `src/admin/admin.repository.ts`, `src/urls/urls.service.ts`, `src/admin/admin.service.ts`.
- LOW: `src/shared/result.ts` (pure type + 2 constructors, no logic, no `any`).
- Transport-only refactor — no new route, input, env var, secret, crypto, or external call. No new attack surface.

### Threat Model Summary (STRIDE — delta only)
| Component | Threat considered | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| 4 P2002 create seams | **Tampering** — catch swallows a non-P2002 error and returns success/err | NOT POSSIBLE — predicate narrows to `instanceof PrismaClientKnownRequestError && code==='P2002'`; everything else `throw error` |
| register / OAuth create | **Information Disclosure** — new enumeration oracle (distinct msg/status for duplicate) | NONE — same `ConflictError` strings → same 409 → byte-identical body |
| OAuth create vs link (G6) | **Elevation of Privilege** — account takeover via link path regression | INTACT — `guardUniqueGoogleId` still wraps `linkGoogleAccount`; removed only from create call site |
| login / findByHash / findByEmail | **Spoofing/timing** — H4 constant-time path altered | UNTOUCHED — not in diff; no bcrypt/compare line changed |
| refresh-token reuse (ADR-012) | **Repudiation/replay** — token family logic regressed | UNAFFECTED — `auth.repository.ts` not in diff |

### Checklist findings (each with evidence)

**1. P2002 narrowing — no swallow of other errors. PASS.**
All four converted methods use the identical predicate and rethrow everything else. Verbatim from the diff:
- `users.repository.ts` (`create` AND `createFromOAuth`), `urls.repository.ts` (`create`), `admin.repository.ts` (`addBlockedDomain`): each catch is
  `if (isUniqueViolation(error)) { return err(new ConflictError(...)); } throw error;`
  where `isUniqueViolation` = `error instanceof Prisma.PrismaClientKnownRequestError && error.code === 'P2002'`.
- Consequence: P2003 (FK), P2025 (row absent), any other `PrismaClientKnownRequestError`, and all connection/unknown errors are **rethrown unchanged** — never converted to `err`, never masked as ConflictError. No swallow. No finding.

**2. No new enumeration oracle. PASS.**
- `register()` (auth.service.ts:75–82): the pre-existing `findByEmail` → `throw new ConflictError('Email address is already registered')` runs BEFORE create (unchanged). The create-path is a race backstop; its err now carries the **same** string `'Email address is already registered'` (users.repository.ts create). A duplicate-email attacker sees the identical ConflictError → 409 → identical body as before. No new distinguishable response. No oracle introduced.
- `createOAuthAccount`: err message is `'This Google account cannot be linked'` — **byte-identical** to the string `guardUniqueGoogleId` throws (auth.service.ts:222 `throw new ConflictError('This Google account cannot be linked')`). Confirmed equal character-for-character.
- Ladder ordering UNCHANGED (auth.service.ts:131–148): G1 google_id-first lookup (133) → G4 unverified-email reject (140) → email-based link (145) → create (148). Only the create unwrap mechanism changed; the ladder is identical.

**3. No timing change on a security-sensitive path. PASS.**
- `login`, `findByHash`, `findByEmail` (H4 constant-time bcrypt / enumeration-timing parity) do NOT appear in the diff. `auth.service.ts` changes are confined to `register` (78–88) and `createOAuthAccount` (186–206) — neither touches bcrypt.compare or the timing path. Create paths are not auth/timing-oracle-sensitive (object creation, not credential verification). No finding.

**4. OAuth create/link parity — G6 takeover defense. PASS (critical item).**
- CREATE (`createFromOAuth`) converted → repo returns `err(ConflictError('This Google account cannot be linked'))` on UNIQUE(google_id)/UNIQUE(email) P2002; service unwraps `if(!r.ok) throw r.error` → ConflictError (auth.service.ts:202–204).
- LINK (`linkGoogleAccount`) NOT converted — `linkExistingAccount` (auth.service.ts:162–173) still wraps the write in `guardUniqueGoogleId(...)` (167–169), and `guardUniqueGoogleId` (217–226) is **STILL PRESENT** and still maps P2002→ConflictError. The null-count race path still maps to `ConflictError('This account is already linked to a different Google identity')` (170–171). guardUniqueGoogleId was removed ONLY from the create call site, exactly as specified.
- Tests: `npx vitest run src/auth/google-oauth.service.test.ts` → **12 passed (12)**, file unmodified (0 edits per backend-dev receipt; confirmed absent from `git diff --name-only`). CREATE-conflict (~208), LINK-conflict (~243), and the non-P2002 propagation test (~234, `createFromOAuth.mockRejectedValueOnce(boom)` asserting `boom` propagates un-masked) all pass — proving non-P2002 still throws through the new repo catch.

**5. ADR-012 (refresh-token reuse detection). UNAFFECTED — by construction.**
`src/auth/auth.repository.ts` does NOT appear in `git diff --name-only HEAD` (changed set: admin.repo/service[+test], auth.service[+test], urls.repo/service[+test], users.repo). `findByHash`/`createToken`/`revokeById`/`revokeFamily` are untouched. ADR-012 reuse-detection is unaffected.

### OWASP Coverage
| Category | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| A01 Broken Access Control | PASS | No authz logic touched; OAuth G1/G4/G6 ladder intact |
| A02 Cryptographic Failures | PASS | No crypto/bcrypt line altered; H4 timing path untouched |
| A03 Injection | PASS | Prisma parameterized; repos remain only Prisma importers |
| A04 Insecure Design | PASS | G6 takeover backstop preserved on both create & link |
| A07 Auth Failures | PASS | login/findByHash/findByEmail untouched; same ConflictError → same 409 |
| A09 Logging Failures | PASS | No log lines added; ConflictError messages carry no PII/secret |
| A10 SSRF | N/A | No URL/network input in this refactor |

### Dependencies
No package.json / lockfile change in this diff. No new dependency, no version bump → no new CVE surface introduced by this refactor. (Full `npm audit` out of scope for a transport-only refactor with zero dependency delta.)

### Security ADRs
None required. ADR-044 (architecture, USER-ratified Option B) already documents the create-seam boundary; no security-specific decision is non-obvious here.

### Verdict
**DONE — security CLEAR for this gate.** Zero Critical, zero High, zero Medium, zero Low findings. The refactor is transport-only: error narrowing is correct (P2002-only → err, all else rethrown), no enumeration oracle introduced (byte-identical ConflictError strings/status), the G6 OAuth takeover backstop is preserved on both create (unwrap) and link (guardUniqueGoogleId), no auth/timing path was modified, and ADR-012 is unaffected (auth.repository.ts untouched). OAuth parity tests 12/12 green.
