**Root cause (refactor-introduced, confirmed via git diff + lcov DA):** the refactor MOVED the P2002 catch from the SERVICE (where service unit tests exercised it via `mockRejectedValue(uniqueViolation())`) INTO the repo. The service unit tests now mock the whole repo (`mockResolvedValue(err(...))`), so they no longer drive the REAL repo catch. Only google-oauth.service.test.ts (real fake-prisma) covers `createFromOAuth`'s err branch + admin integration covers admin's err branch. NO test drives the real `urls.repository.create` or `users.repository.create` catch, and NO test drives the non-P2002 `throw error` rethrow in any of the four repo methods, nor the `register` create-conflict backstop (the register conflict test hits the earlier `findByEmail` guard @78 and never reaches the create-err unwrap). These are NET-NEW lines/branches (the old repo `create` was a one-liner) → new uncovered code, hence the branch regression. The security parity claim ("non-P2002 rethrown unchanged") is correct in code but is NOT exercised by a real-repo test for urls/users/admin.

**This is a coverage finding, NOT a behavior bug** — all 543 tests pass, every assertion is preserved, route behavior is byte-identical. The gap is missing tests for the relocated catch, not broken logic.

