543/543 pass (exit 0), ALL test edits confirmed transport-only (every assertion SAME), no weakening/deletion/skips, exactly 3 files changed (google-oauth untouched, 12/12), non-P2002 parity tests intact. BUT overall branch coverage dropped 96.94%→96.75% (below baseline) due to relocated-but-untested repo catch branches → trips the baseline-degradation P1 rule. Per my STATUS gate ("DONE only if ... coverage not dropped"), this is **NEEDS_REVIEW**, not DONE. Recommend quality-lead weigh: coverage is still >>threshold (85%) and the gap is missing-tests-for-correct-logic, not a behavior defect — likely shippable with a follow-up to add real-repo P2002/non-P2002 tests (or accept as known_debt). Defer to code-quality's parallel baseline read + quality-lead's go/no-go.

