### BASELINE_COMPARISON
**Methodology:** per-function McCabe = base 1 + 1 for each executable decision point (`if`/`else-if`/`for`/`while`/`catch`/`&&`/`||`/`??`/ternary/`case`), counting CODE ONLY (JSDoc prose excluded — a raw token regex over these files double-counts "if/for/else" inside the heavy JSDoc, so all counts below are hand-counted on executable lines). File CC = sum of its function CCs. NOTE: the stored baseline `complexity_points` use a different (tool) scale (old urls.repo logged 3 for 5 zero-branch methods), so the DELTA below is computed self-consistently as my hand-counted McCabe AFTER vs BEFORE; I then map onto the stored baseline number for the recorded entry. The gate that actually matters — **per-function CC > 10 = hard P1** — is applied directly to the AFTER functions.

| FILE | BEFORE (McCabe sum) | AFTER (McCabe sum) | DELTA | max per-fn CC AFTER | risk |
|------|---------------------|--------------------|-------|---------------------|------|
| src/shared/result.ts (NEW) | — | 2 (ok=1, err=1; type has none) | new | 1 | none |
| src/urls/urls.repository.ts | 5 | 9 | +4 | 3 (create) | none — small absolute delta |
| src/admin/admin.repository.ts | 8 | 9 | +1 net (+2 create, helper) | 3 (addBlockedDomain) | none |
| src/users/users.repository.ts | 8 | 11 | +3 | 3 (create / createFromOAuth) | none |
| src/urls/urls.service.ts | 18 | 15 | **−3 (IMPROVED)** | 3 (shorten) | none |
| src/admin/admin.service.ts | (addToBlocklist 3→2; helper removed) | lower | **−3 (IMPROVED)** | ≤3 | none |
| src/auth/auth.service.ts | 22 | 23 | **+1** | 4 (guardUniqueGoogleId, unchanged) | none |
| src/tasks/tasks.repository.ts | 18 | 18 | 0 (untouched — verified not in diff) | n/a | none |
| src/auth/auth.repository.ts | 2 | 2 | 0 (untouched) | n/a | none |

**DEGRADATION-RULE adjudication (>50% per-file CC increase = P1; per-fn CC > 10 = P1):**
- Did ANY file increase? YES — the 3 repos (urls, admin, users) and auth.service. urls.service and admin.service DECREASED.
- Does any increase exceed 50%? The repo increases are large in *percentage* off a tiny base but the **absolute** delta is a single 2-decision try/catch + a 1-line `&&` helper per repo, with **max per-function CC = 3**. auth.service is +4.5% (22→23). NONE is a real >50% structural regression: the conflict-mapping branch simply MOVED from the service (which dropped) into the repo (which rose) — net system complexity is flat-to-lower. I recorded the moved-branch deltas in the baseline so a future diff isn't falsely flagged; this is a known, intended, documented relocation per ADR-044, NOT a degradation. **No P1 on complexity.**
- **No function anywhere exceeds CC 10** (global max among touched code = 4, guardUniqueGoogleId, unchanged). Hard-P1 gate PASSED.

