### Dependencies
No new dependencies (orchestrator constraint confirmed). npm audit posture unchanged from the shipped baseline; nothing to re-audit for this feature.

### Security ADRs (new, start at ADR-045 — decisions.md ends at ADR-044)
- **ADR-045** Audit-log immutability is dual-layer (app: no update/delete surface; DB: Postgres BEFORE UPDATE/DELETE trigger RAISE) + no User→audit cascade (actor_id ON DELETE SET NULL) — the audit log is a forensic artifact whose integrity is a security control, so the app DB account is treated as a potential adversary.
- **ADR-046** Audit metadata is a strict non-sensitive allowlist; the SAME redaction set as logger.ts applies; audit carries actorId never provider `sub` (extends ADR-040); the service fails safe (typed fields / redaction pass, never an arbitrary blob).
- **ADR-047** Audit retention/PII stance: ip_address+user_agent are PII retained under legitimate-interest security basis with a defined horizon; user deletion nulls actor_id but does not delete the forensic row (erasure tension documented); purge job deferred.

### SECURITY REQUIREMENTS CHECKLIST (backend-dev + db-engineer MUST satisfy; quality-lead verifies)
- [ ] **S1 (F1, HIGH)** GET /audit-logs is behind plugin-wide `authGuard` + `requireRole(UserRole.ADMIN)` (copy src/admin/admin.routes.ts:91-92). Non-admin → 403. No self-service / per-user read branch.
- [ ] **S2 (F3, HIGH)** actor_id = `requireAuth(request).userId` (JWT sub) or null; NEVER from request body. Provide a single shared `requestContext(request)` helper.
- [ ] **S3 (F3, HIGH)** ip_address = Fastify `request.ip` (honours trustProxy at app.ts:50); do NOT hand-parse x-forwarded-for. user_agent = `request.headers['user-agent']`, capped ≤512 chars, stored opaque.
- [ ] **S4 (F2, HIGH)** metadata = allowlisted non-sensitive identifiers ONLY. Forbidden: password/hash, any token/JWT, code_verifier/PKCE state, Google sub/id_token/client_secret, raw bodies/headers, auth/cookie values. Service accepts a typed object (never an arbitrary blob) + redaction pass before INSERT (fail safe).
- [ ] **S5 (F4, HIGH)** No UPDATE/DELETE endpoints; repository exposes insert + read only.
- [ ] **S6 (F4, HIGH — db-engineer)** Migration 006 adds a Postgres `BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE ON audit_logs` trigger that RAISEs (verified on a real Postgres instance + documented). qa adds a fake-prisma auditLog delegate that rejects update/delete.
- [ ] **S7 (F4, HIGH — db-engineer)** actor_id has NO cascading delete from User (ON DELETE SET NULL or non-FK UUID) — audit rows survive user deletion.
- [ ] **S8 (F5, MED)** Fire-and-forget: audit INSERT failure does NOT fail the main op, BUT is caught and `log.error({event:'AUDIT_WRITE_FAILED',...})`. Never blocking/synchronous in the request critical path.
- [ ] **S9 (F6, MED)** All filters Zod-validated: event_type ∈ AuditAction enum; actor_id/target_id UUID; date range coerced + reject from>to; pagination max 100; created_at index for newest-first. No `$queryRawUnsafe` / no string-interpolated SQL.
- [ ] **S10 (F7, MED)** Retention/PII stance recorded (ADR-047); no purge job this release (documented).
