### Security Controls Implemented (S1–S12)
- **S1** ✅ GET /audit-logs behind plugin-wide authGuard + requireRole(UserRole.ADMIN) (copied admin.routes.ts:91-92); actor_id is a filter, no per-user self-service branch.
- **S2** ✅ actorId = request.authContext?.userId (JWT sub) via the single requestContext() helper; for public auth routes the actor is the server-resolved auth-result id, NEVER a body field.
- **S3** ✅ ip = request.ip (honours trustProxy app.ts:50, no x-forwarded-for parsing); userAgent = headers['user-agent'].slice(0,512).
- **S4** ✅ metadata built ONLY from the typed AuditFields allowlist (outcome/family/jti/reason/count); FORBIDDEN_METADATA_KEYS redaction pass (logger REDACT_PATHS + code_verifier/state/sub/client_secret/id_token) drops any forbidden key before INSERT.
- **S5** ✅ repository exposes insert + read ONLY; no update/delete method.
- **S6/S7** — db-engineer (verified on real PG16); fake-prisma update/delete THROW mirrors it app-side.
- **S8** ✅ fire-and-forget: record() sync/void, fires insert without await, single `.catch`→log.error(AUDIT_WRITE_FAILED); never throws, never fails the main op.
- **S9** ✅ all filters Zod-validated; Prisma parameterized builder (no $queryRawUnsafe); limit cap 100; from≤to refine.
- **S10** — retention stance ADR-047 (recorded; no purge job).
- **S11** ✅ ok() envelope + sanitized global error handler; response DTO (AuditLogResponse) exposes only intended fields.
- **S12** ✅ extended the EXISTING AUDIT_ACTION enum (no duplication); DB sink is ADDITIVE to the logger audit() — both run.

### AUDIT_ACTION additions
TASK_BULK_CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE, URL_APPROVED, URL_REJECTED, USER_ROLE_CHANGED. NOTE: USER_ROLE_CHANGED is defined for vocabulary completeness but NOT emitted — no role-change endpoint exists in the codebase today (role is set only by the register default + OAuth ladder). Documented for tech-writer/future.

