### ADR Conformance (verified against source)
- **ADR-049 (integration seam):** ✅ PASS. `AuditSink` is a pure-types port in shared/audit-sink.ts (imports only AuditAction/AuditFields; zero Fastify, zero feature import). `record()` is sync/`void`, fires `this.repo.insert(row)` WITHOUT await; the **single** try/catch is the detached `.catch` in the sink impl (service.ts:164–169 → logs AUDIT_WRITE_FAILED, never swallowed, never re-thrown). NO `FastifyRequest` in any service signature — routes call `requestContext(request)` and pass the plain `RequestContext` POJO down. NOOP_AUDIT_SINK default on all 4 route plugins. Wired once in app.ts:138 (one AuditService instance as both sink and read service). CLEAN.
- **ADR-046 (metadata allowlist + redaction):** ✅ PASS. `buildMetadata` assembles metadata ONLY from the typed AuditFields allowlist (outcome/family/jti/reason/count), then a fail-safe pass drops any key in `FORBIDDEN_METADATA_KEYS` (logger REDACT_PATHS + code_verifier/state/sub/googleSub/id_token/client_secret, both snake+camel). actorId/targetId/targetType are columned separately, never duplicated into metadata. Redaction present and correct.
- **ADR-044 (Result boundary):** ✅ PASS. Repository reads return plain `T|null`/array shapes (findMany → `{rows,total}`); `insert` returns `Promise<void>` NOT a Result — correct per ADR-049 (fire-and-forget write has no recoverable conflict to branch on). No Result imported in the audit module, consistent with the ADR-044 "convert ONLY the throw-on-failure create seam" ruling.
- **ADR-010 (layering):** ✅ PASS. audit.repository.ts is the ONLY Prisma importer in src/audit (service/routes/schemas import zero `@prisma/client` runtime — service imports only `@prisma/client` *types* AuditLog/AuditTargetType/Prisma, which is type-only and conventional). Service is Fastify-free (takes FastifyBaseLogger as an injected logger interface only — consistent with existing services; no request/reply). Routes own the Zod parse (`parseOrThrow(auditQuerySchema, ...)`). Downward-only deps intact: routes→service→repository→Prisma.

